IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mt-ui`

-- Montana unemployment insurance -- the claimant's seat. Plain inputs, each question calls the core in mt-ui.l4.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Montana unemployment insurance -- the claimant's questions`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, e IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Quarterly wages`
`my five quarters` a b c d e MEANS
    `Quarterly wages` WITH
        `quarter 1 (oldest)` IS a
        `quarter 2` IS b
        `quarter 3` IS c
        `quarter 4` IS d
        `quarter 5 (most recent)` IS e

§§ `Do I qualify, and for how much`

@export Do my wages qualify me for Montana unemployment benefits, and on which base period (39-51-201(2), 39-51-2105)?
GIVEN `wages in the 5th most recent completed quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid to you in covered employment in the oldest of the last 5 completed calendar quarters before you file
      `wages in the 4th most recent completed quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `wages in the 3rd most recent completed quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `wages in the 2nd most recent completed quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `wages in the most recent completed quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the last completed calendar quarter before you file
      `the average annual wage` IS A NUMBER @desc Montana's average annual wage for the year, as computed by the department under 39-51-2201(2)
GIVETH A `Which base period`
`Do my wages qualify me for benefits` MEANS
    `the base period that qualifies` (`my five quarters` `wages in the 5th most recent completed quarter` `wages in the 4th most recent completed quarter` `wages in the 3rd most recent completed quarter` `wages in the 2nd most recent completed quarter` `wages in the most recent completed quarter`) `the average annual wage`

@export What is my weekly benefit amount (39-51-2201)? Nothing if my wages do not qualify.
GIVEN `my wages 5 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid to you in covered employment in the oldest of the last 5 completed calendar quarters before you file
      `my wages 4 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `my wages 3 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `my wages 2 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `my wages last quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the last completed calendar quarter before you file
      `average annual wage` IS A NUMBER @desc Montana's average annual wage for the year, as computed by the department under 39-51-2201(2)
      `contribution schedule I is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the unemployment insurance contribution schedule in force under 39-51-1218 is Schedule I (the lowest); if Schedule II or higher, answer no
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my weekly benefit amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the qualifying base period wages` (`my five quarters` `my wages 5 quarters back` `my wages 4 quarters back` `my wages 3 quarters back` `my wages 2 quarters back` `my wages last quarter`) `average annual wage`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST bp THEN JUST (`the weekly benefit amount` bp `average annual wage` `contribution schedule I is in force`)

@export How many weeks of benefits, and what total, can I get in my benefit year (39-51-2204)? Nothing if my wages do not qualify.
GIVEN `wages 5 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid to you in covered employment in the oldest of the last 5 completed calendar quarters before you file
      `wages 4 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `wages 3 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `wages 2 quarters back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `wages last quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the last completed calendar quarter before you file
      `Montana average annual wage` IS A NUMBER @desc Montana's average annual wage for the year, as computed by the department under 39-51-2201(2)
      `schedule I in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contribution schedule in force under 39-51-1218 is Schedule I
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What is my maximum benefit amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the qualifying base period wages` (`my five quarters` `wages 5 quarters back` `wages 4 quarters back` `wages 3 quarters back` `wages 2 quarters back` `wages last quarter`) `Montana average annual wage`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST bp THEN JUST ((`the weekly benefit amount` bp `Montana average annual wage` `schedule I in force`) TIMES (`the full weeks of benefits` bp))

@export How many full weeks of benefits can I get (39-51-2204)? Nothing if my wages do not qualify.
GIVEN `quarter wages 5 back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid to you in covered employment in the oldest of the last 5 completed calendar quarters before you file
      `quarter wages 4 back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `quarter wages 3 back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `quarter wages 2 back` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the next quarter
      `quarter wages last` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages paid in the last completed calendar quarter before you file
      `the state average annual wage` IS A NUMBER @desc Montana's average annual wage for the year, as computed by the department under 39-51-2201(2)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How many weeks of benefits can I get` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the qualifying base period wages` (`my five quarters` `quarter wages 5 back` `quarter wages 4 back` `quarter wages 3 back` `quarter wages 2 back` `quarter wages last`) `the state average annual wage`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST bp THEN JUST (`the full weeks of benefits` bp)

-- This group only arises if you have lost your job or been offered work while claiming.
§§ `How I lost my job, and job offers (if this has happened to you)`

@export Am I disqualified because of how my last job ended (39-51-2302, 39-51-2303)?
GIVEN `how my job ended` IS A `How the job ended` @desc How your last job ended, as the department finds: laid off for lack of work; quit with or without good cause attributable to the employment; discharged, not for misconduct, for misconduct, for gross misconduct, or for failing or refusing an employer drug test under a written policy
      `an exception for quitting applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you quit for one of the 39-51-2302(2) reasons: illness or injury on medical advice and offered to return on recovery; left temporary work to go back to your regular employer; a military order of under 180 days after which your job had ended; or your spouse's mandatory military transfer
      `I have attended school for 3 months since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been in regular attendance at an accredited Montana educational institution for at least 3 consecutive months since you quit
      `the drug test was for marijuana and I hold a registry card` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the drug test was for marijuana and you are a registered medical marijuana cardholder
      `my weekly benefit amount` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount
GIVETH A `Disqualification`
`Am I disqualified by how my job ended` MEANS
    `the disqualification for the separation` `how my job ended` `an exception for quitting applies` `I have attended school for 3 months since` `the drug test was for marijuana and I hold a registry card` `my weekly benefit amount`

@export If I turn down this job offer, will I lose benefits (39-51-2304)?
GIVEN `the job is open because of a strike or lockout` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the job is vacant directly because of a strike, lockout or other labor dispute
      `the job is substantially worse than local prevailing terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether its wages, hours or conditions are substantially less favorable to you than those prevailing for similar work in the area
      `the job requires a company union or no union` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would have to join a company union, or resign from or not join a genuine labor union
      `the department finds the job suitable for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the department finds the work suitable, weighing risk to health and safety, your fitness and training, experience and earnings, length of unemployment and local prospects, and distance
      `weeks I have been unemployed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks you have been unemployed
      `offered pay compared with my old pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The offered pay as a fraction of your earnings in previous insured work in your usual occupation (for example 0.8 for 80%)
      `the offer is below the federal minimum wage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offered pay is below the federal minimum wage
      `I have good cause to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have good cause for refusing, as the department finds
      `my weekly benefit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount
GIVETH A `Refusal outcome`
`Will I lose benefits if I refuse this job` MEANS
    `the outcome of refusing the offer`
        (`Job offer` WITH
            `the vacancy is due directly to a strike, lockout or other labor dispute`          IS `the job is open because of a strike or lockout`
            `pay, hours or conditions are substantially less favorable than prevailing locally` IS `the job is substantially worse than local prevailing terms`
            `the job requires joining a company union or not joining a bona fide union`         IS `the job requires a company union or no union`
            `the department finds it suitable on the 39-51-2304(2) factors`                     IS `the department finds the job suitable for me`
            `weeks of unemployment so far`                                                       IS `weeks I have been unemployed`
            `offered pay as a fraction of my previous insured earnings in my customary occupation` IS `offered pay compared with my old pay`
            `the offered pay is below the federal minimum wage`                                  IS `the offer is below the federal minimum wage`)
        `I have good cause to refuse`
        `my weekly benefit`

§§ `Each week I claim`

@export How much will I be paid for this week of unemployment (39-51-2101, 39-51-2104, 39-51-2202, 39-51-2203)?
GIVEN `my weekly benefit amount for the week` IS A NUMBER @desc Your weekly benefit amount
      `hours I worked this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Hours you worked in the week (Sunday to Saturday)
      `wages I earned this week` IS A NUMBER @desc Wages you earned in the week, before tax
      `I worked fewer hours than usual for lack of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any work you did this week was fewer hours than you usually work, because there was not enough work
      `days I was unavailable for work` IS A NUMBER @desc Days, or parts of days, this week you were not available for work although work was available
      `pension to deduct this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly share of a pension or retirement pay from a base-period employer's plan that must be deducted under 39-51-2203 (0 if none, or if you paid directly into the fund it comes from)
      `I filed my weekly claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you filed your claim and continued claim for the week as the department requires
      `I was able, available and looking for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were able to work, available for work and seeking work
      `I have served my waiting week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already served the 1-week unpaid waiting period
      `I am registered with job service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered for work with your local job service office (or excused from it)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much will I be paid for this week` MEANS
    `the payment for the week`
        (`The week` WITH
            `hours worked in the week`                               IS `hours I worked this week`
            `wages earned in the week`                               IS `wages I earned this week`
            `worked fewer hours than usual because of a lack of work` IS `I worked fewer hours than usual for lack of work`
            `days or part-days unavailable for work in the week`     IS `days I was unavailable for work`
            `pension reasonably attributable to the week that must be deducted` IS `pension to deduct this week`
            `filed the claim and continued claims as the rules require`    IS `I filed my weekly claim`
            `able to work, available for work and seeking work`            IS `I was able, available and looking for work`
            `has served the 1-week waiting period`                         IS `I have served my waiting week`
            `registered for work with the local job service, or excused`  IS `I am registered with job service`)
        `my weekly benefit amount for the week`

-- This group only arises if you were paid for a week and then got workers' compensation or other UI for it.
§§ `Paying back (if this has happened to you)`

@export Must I repay unemployment benefits for a week I was later paid workers' compensation or other unemployment benefits for (39-51-2306(2))?
GIVEN `I was later paid workers' compensation or other unemployment benefits for a week already paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after receiving Montana benefits for a week, you received workers' compensation disability pay or other state or federal unemployment benefits for that same week
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I repay the benefits for that week` IF
    `must repay the week` `I was later paid workers' compensation or other unemployment benefits for a week already paid`
